{"type":"app","meta":{"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/about/layout,_N_T_/about/page,_N_T_/about"},"segmentPaths":["/_tree","/_full","/about/__PAGE__","/about","/_index","/_head"]},"html":"<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charSet=\"utf-8\"/><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"/><link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/images/artist.jpg\"/><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/_next/static/chunks/1-tw417awgvza.css\" data-precedence=\"next\"/><link rel=\"preload\" as=\"script\" fetchPriority=\"low\" href=\"/_next/static/chunks/046rkacd53sxw.js\"/><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/1zp2o36e3749-.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/2us7qv_uq7h07.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/2ejk_26znfoeu.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/3nc6x0_y5iwnk.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/turbopack-1p52jldn8i60q.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/0dga69b6f-6u0.js\" async=\"\"></script><title>Pattachitra | Traditional Art of Odisha</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Explore the traditional Pattachitra art of Odisha, its history, paintings, artists, culture, and heritage.\"/><meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"Pattachitra,Pattachitra art,Odisha art,traditional art of Odisha,Pattachitra paintings,Indian traditional art\"/><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\"/><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico?favicon.2vob68tjqpejf.ico\" sizes=\"256x256\" type=\"image/x-icon\"/><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/0cz1d0mv5g_q7.js\" noModule=\"\"></script></head><body><div hidden=\"\"><!--$--><!--/$--></div><nav class=\"navbar\"><a class=\"logo\" href=\"/\">PATTACHITRA</a><ul class=\"nav-links\"><li><a class=\"\" href=\"/\">Home</a></li><li><a class=\"active\" href=\"/about\">About</a></li><li><a class=\"\" href=\"/gallery\">Gallery</a></li><li><a class=\"\" href=\"/contact\">Contact</a></li></ul><button class=\"hamburger \" aria-label=\"Toggle menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></nav><div class=\"mobile-menu \"><ul><li><a class=\"\" href=\"/\">Home</a></li><li><a class=\"active\" href=\"/about\">About</a></li><li><a class=\"\" href=\"/gallery\">Gallery</a></li><li><a class=\"\" href=\"/contact\">Contact</a></li></ul></div><main class=\"about-page\"><div class=\"about-header\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Our Heritage</span><h1>About the Artist</h1><p>A life devoted to preserving Odisha&#x27;s most sacred visual tradition.</p></div><section class=\"story\"><div class=\"story-img\"><img src=\"/images/artist.jpg\" alt=\"The artist at work\"/></div><div class=\"story-text\"><span class=\"story-eyebrow\">A Life Dedicated to Art</span><h3>From Raghurajpur to the World</h3><p>Growing up in Raghurajpur — one of India&#x27;s heritage craft villages — I watched my grandfather transform simple cotton cloth into vivid mythological worlds. The rhythm of his brush became my lullaby, and by age fifteen, I was painting my own scrolls.</p><p>Pattachitra is more than art; it is devotion. Each pigment is ground from natural materials — conch shells for white, lampblack for deep outlines, hingula for vermilion red. The process itself is a meditation.</p><p>Today I work to honour this lineage while exploring contemporary themes, bridging the ancient and the modern so that Pattachitra continues to live and breathe in a new age.</p></div></section><section class=\"journey\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Milestones</span><h2>The Journey</h2><div class=\"timeline\"><div class=\"timeline-line\"></div><div class=\"timeline-item\"><div class=\"timeline-marker\"><span class=\"timeline-dot\"></span></div><div class=\"timeline-card\"><span class=\"year\">2002</span><p class=\"event\">Began formal training under master artisan Guru Ananta Maharana</p></div></div><div class=\"timeline-item\"><div class=\"timeline-marker\"><span class=\"timeline-dot\"></span></div><div class=\"timeline-card\"><span class=\"year\">2012</span><p class=\"event\">First solo exhibition at the National Gallery of Modern Art, New Delhi</p></div></div><div class=\"timeline-item\"><div class=\"timeline-marker\"><span class=\"timeline-dot\"></span></div><div class=\"timeline-card\"><span class=\"year\">2016</span><p class=\"event\">Awarded the State Handicrafts Award for excellence in Pattachitra</p></div></div><div class=\"timeline-item\"><div class=\"timeline-marker\"><span class=\"timeline-dot\"></span></div><div class=\"timeline-card\"><span class=\"year\">2020</span><p class=\"event\">Featured in international exhibitions across London, Tokyo, and New York</p></div></div><div class=\"timeline-item\"><div class=\"timeline-marker\"><span class=\"timeline-dot\"></span></div><div class=\"timeline-card\"><span class=\"year\">2024</span><p class=\"event\">Launched online platform to bring Pattachitra art to global collectors</p></div></div></div></section><section class=\"awards\"><span class=\"eyebrow center\">Recognition</span><h2>Honoured Moments</h2><div class=\"award-grid\"><div class=\"award-card\"><div class=\"award-body\"><div class=\"award-top\"><strong>Odisha State Award for Folk Art Painting</strong><span class=\"award-year\">2016</span></div><p>Recognized by the Government of Odisha for excellence in traditional Pattachitra painting.</p></div></div><div class=\"award-card\"><div class=\"award-body\"><div class=\"award-top\"><strong>Basant Utsav Award</strong><span class=\"award-year\">2017</span></div><p>Honored for outstanding contributions to Odisha&#x27;s folk art heritage.</p></div></div><div class=\"award-card\"><div class=\"award-body\"><div class=\"award-top\"><strong>Pattachitra HastaShilpi Award</strong><span class=\"award-year\">2022</span></div><p>Awarded for exceptional craftsmanship in traditional Pattachitra art.</p></div></div><div class=\"award-card\"><div class=\"award-body\"><div class=\"award-top\"><strong>Odisha Folk Artist Award</strong><span class=\"award-year\">2024</span></div><p>Recognized for preserving and promoting Odisha&#x27;s traditional folk art.</p></div></div></div></section></main><!--$--><!--/$--><footer class=\"footer\"><div class=\"footer-inner\"><h2>Pattachitra Art • Odisha</h2><p>Preserving the ancient art of storytelling through colours and brushstrokes.</p><p class=\"artwork-rights\">&quot;All artworks displayed on this website are original creations by the artist. Please respect the artist&#x27;s work by not reproducing or using these artworks without permission.&quot;</p><p class=\"copy\">© 2026 All rights reserved</p></div></footer><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/046rkacd53sxw.js\" id=\"_R_\" async=\"\"></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1:\\\"$Sreact.fragment\\\"\\n2:I[162319,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n3:I[339756,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n4:I[837457,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n5:I[347257,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\\\"],\\\"ClientPageRoot\\\"]\\n6:I[360078,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0dga69b6f-6u0.js\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n9:I[897367,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\\\"],\\\"OutletBoundary\\\"]\\na:\\\"$Sreact.suspense\\\"\\nd:I[897367,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0l8fzc8sdyuv9.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1ntn7efqc-iiw.js\\\"],\\\